WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:10.030
61. Easter Island If you wanted to get as far away from other

2
00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:16.990
people as you possibly could, Easter Island would be a good place to go. It's about 2,000

3
00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:23.350
kilometers from its nearest neighbors out in the southern Pacific Ocean. Easter Island

4
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:29.750
is a small triangle about 3,500 kilometers west of Chile. Easter Island is a special

5
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:36.870
territory of Chile. It was discovered by a Dutch explorer in 1722, but it had been

6
00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:42.510
inhabited for about a thousand years before that. Scientists think that the first settlers

7
00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:50.310
on Easter Island came from the Marquesas Islands more than 3,000 kilometers away. Imagine making

8
00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:56.750
that journey in a small canoe. Easter Island is famous for its huge stone statues called

9
00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:03.550
moai that line many of the island's coasts. The moai are statues of men with huge heads

10
00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:11.390
and stern faces. Archaeologists believe the statues represent ancestors. Easter Islanders

11
00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:17.390
put the statues up to allow the ancestors to continue to watch over their lands. The

12
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:25.550
moai were made between AD 1100 and AD 1688. Amazingly, Easter Islanders used only hand

13
00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:33.150
tools like chisels to make them. Some of these statues weighed more than 80 tons. Archaeologists

14
00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:39.070
aren't sure how these statues were moved. It must have taken many people working together

15
00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:45.750
to transport them. In addition to the moai, Easter Island has other stone carvings, stone

16
00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:51.950
buildings and wood carvings. This unique culture developed its own written language, though

17
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:58.670
most of it has been lost. Easter Island has suffered many tragedies, including war, hunger,

18
00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:05.710
slavery, disease and environmental disasters. It can be difficult to be so far from the

19
00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:12.630
rest of the world. But Easter Islanders seem hardy and strong like their statues. They

20
00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:18.190
are preserving their ancient culture while connecting more and more with the outside

21
00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:18.830
world.
